    <statement><p>Find the gradient of the given function. Assume the variables
are restricted to a domain on which the function is defined.
<me>z = \left(5x+y\right)e^{2y}</me></p>
<p><m>\nabla z =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5e^{2y}\boldsymbol{i}+\left(1+2\mathopen{}\left(5x+y\right)\right)e^{2y}\boldsymbol{j}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>z_x = 5e^{2y}\quad \mbox{and}\quad z_y = \left(1+2\mathopen{}\left(5x+y\right)\right)e^{2y},</me>
we have
<me>\nabla z = 5e^{2y}\boldsymbol{i}+\left(1+2\mathopen{}\left(5x+y\right)\right)e^{2y}\boldsymbol{j}.</me>



</solution>
